Z||000026||84Bill||08-01-2001||11:11 AM||||Oh yeah? I call ya out man.. ::cracking knuckels::<P>All I have to say is "nothing is perfect" no matter how small and restrictive something is you will <B>always</B> have 1 or 2 in the bunch. Even on a "pay" forum your still going to have em. bann them and someone else will take their place. <BR>The Borg had the idea right off the bat "resistance is futile" once applied to everyday life then you will see how much easier it is to live with. <BR>The whotoo's will always rebell, the idiots will still annoy and the slow drivers will always be in the left lane. Thats just life my friend. The only escape is to be hit with an O2 bottle in an MRI machine or move in with maniak84. <BR>I personaly like to call a spade a spade and that rule has been applied to myself as well. There are some people that get their jolies pissing off other people. I like to trow mud at them on occasion but for the most part sticks and stones ect. ect.<BR>So I guess what I'm trying to get across is, don't let them get to you. The best defence is to be like vapor, that really pisses them off.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Philphine||08-01-2001||11:40 AM||||i changed my name a while back, but it was because this was the first thing i joined on the internet and i kinda filled the form out wrong. like others, i use just this name not only here, but everywhere on the internet i can (i guess it's wierd enough that no one else wants it). i hope that even if someone used it somewhere else where i'm not registered for what ever reason (trouble or fun), it would be obvious to someone who's seen what i've written on the net before to know it's not me. like in real life, i think of it as protecting my good name and reputation.<P>i have a few times been very upset with things i've read here and left the forum. i didn't post about it 'cause i know 1 monkey dosen't stop the show. i cool down or the thread finally fades away and i start posting again.<P>as for trolls and people who insult for fun or are just really insensitive, i try to just let that go. i don't understand joining a forum when you don't have the car or whatever the forum focuses on or any positive interest in it. i have a lot more trouble with that on another forum. in fact i guess i'm sometimes considered the troll.<P>i'm rambling, but thats just some stuff i've been thinking. it's wierd. if i had to give up all but one car i'd most likely keep my chevy. but if i made that choice by which forum i like best i'd be keeping a fiero. <P>try and keep it light yall.<P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
